Don't build the udmabuf test helpers when <linux/udmabuf.h> is unavailable

The udmabuf uapi header only exists since Linux 5.19. Distributions (and
packaging systems) that deliberately build against older kernel uapi headers
for binary compatibility must be able to build without it, so only compile
udmabuftestutils.cpp when the header is actually present. The helpers are only
used by the udmabuf unit tests, which are skipped anyway when the feature
check for linux_dmabuf fails.

diff --git a/src/multimediatestlib/CMakeLists.txt b/src/multimediatestlib/CMakeLists.txt
index 68d48a1..0000000 100644
--- a/src/multimediatestlib/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/multimediatestlib/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -36,7 +36,11 @@ qt_internal_add_module(MultimediaTestLibPrivate
     QT_LICENSE_ID QT_COMMERCIAL_OR_GPL3
 )
 
-qt_internal_extend_target(MultimediaTestLibPrivate CONDITION LINUX
+include(CheckIncludeFileCXX)
+check_include_file_cxx("linux/udmabuf.h" QT_MULTIMEDIA_HAVE_UDMABUF)
+
+qt_internal_extend_target(MultimediaTestLibPrivate
+    CONDITION LINUX AND QT_MULTIMEDIA_HAVE_UDMABUF
     SOURCES
         udmabuftestutils_p.h udmabuftestutils.cpp
 )
